# WHAT THIS KEEPS OUT OF `helm package`, AND WHY EACH LINE IS HERE.
#
# ci/
#   chart/ci/render-values.yaml is tooling input, not chart content: it exists
#   only so the org's release image gate can RENDER a chart whose defaults are
#   deliberately not a valid configuration (nova.url has no default). Its own
#   header says "NOT AN INSTALL EXAMPLE. Do not copy this file." Without this
#   line the next release ships it to every consumer; nobody decided that, it
#   would just ride along.
#
# .helmignore
#   THE SELF-REFERENCE IS LOAD-BEARING. .helmignore is itself packaged, so
#   listing only `ci/` trades one unwanted member for another. Measured with
#   `helm package` of this chart:
#
#       no .helmignore                          31 members (ci/render-values.yaml in)
#       .helmignore listing only `ci/`          31 members (SWAPS it for .helmignore)
#       .helmignore listing `ci/` AND itself    30 members, neither present
#
#   Do not remove this line as a tidy-up: nothing fails, the archive silently
#   regains a member. scripts/validate.py and lint.yaml both check it.
#
# THE RELEASE IMAGE GATE IS UNAFFECTED. chart-images.yaml copies the chart
# DIRECTORY from the repository checkout (not from a package) and passes the
# values file with `-f`, so this file cannot hide ci/render-values.yaml from it.
ci/
.helmignore
